hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"167","It is narrated by Muhammad ibn al-Walid, it is narrated by Abu Amer, it is narrated by Israel, on the authority of Amer, who is the son of Shaqiq ibn Hamza al-Asadi, on the authority of a brother, who is Ibn Salamah. Abu Wael, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan performing ablution three times, and he wiped his head and ears, the tops and insides of them, and washed his feet three times. Three times, he washed his fingertips, combed his beard, and washed his face, and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing the same as you saw me doing."
